From ebb8fb113c9f4e52c16c143d57237e55fd9681f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 02:40:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] NEON i32 max reduction via smax/smaxv + late AArch64
 vectorization pass

AUDITED PORT of levkropp 8b139820 (max reductions) and the 8ef1978f
late-pass concept, rebuilt for our diverged vectorizer rather than
cherry-picked (his diffs no longer apply; our transform has byte-IV
strength reduction and different remainder plumbing).

New pipeline stage: vectorize_function_two_wide_late runs after the
main pass loop's if_convert phase (AArch64, not -Os/-Oz; gates:
CCC_DISABLE_PASSES=latevec or vectorize). Max reductions only exist in
Select form after if-conversion, so the early vectorizer structurally
never sees them (verified: early pass logs 'Rejecting conditional
reduction loop' on the CondBranch form). Idempotent by construction --
already-vectorized loops contain Vec* intrinsics and fail the scalar
shape analyzers. source_spans invalidated by block surgery are dropped
(wrong-line debug info otherwise), then DCE.

Detector (analyze_reduction_pattern): accumulator phi whose latch
incoming is a Select of {phi, loaded element}, cond = signed compare of
element vs phi, all four polarities. SIGNED only -- smax must never
match an unsigned compare (that needs umax). NEON-gated. STRICT shape
gate kept from his version: the access must be a marching-pointer phi
stepping exactly 4 bytes whose preheader incoming is a constant-offset
GEP at iv_init*4 -- coverage legality depends on it, and a direct
IV-indexed GEP would be re-scaled wrong (rejected outright).

Transform: broadcast scalar init into the vector accumulator (zero
vector iterations reduce back to the init -- smaxv of 4 equal lanes),
lane-wise VecSmaxI32x4 in the body, VecHorizontalMaxI32x4 (smaxv) in
vec_exit, marching-pointer step scaled 4->16 bytes. Remainder: scalar
Cmp+Select, start index w*(iv_final - c) RELATIVE to the pointer's
preheader element c, limit shifted to n-c (constant-folded or a Sub on
dynamic limits).

Port bugs found by the adversarial battery and fixed before commit:
1. VecHorizontalMaxI32x4 initially classified as vector-producing;
   its dest then hit ARM callee_saved_name with a vector-reg index ->
   ICE 'invalid ARM register index'. It produces a scalar I32, exactly
   like the VecHorizontalAdd family.
2. The remainder initially addressed relative to the marching-pointer
   PHI -- but as an SSA value read in vec_exit that phi holds the END
   pointer, double-counting vector coverage (out-of-bounds reads for
   large n). Now resolves the phi's preheader incoming.
3. Marching-pointer latch step was left at 4 bytes while the body
   consumed 4 lanes -- every vector load after the first read 3 stale
   lanes. Now scaled to 16 with a debug_assert that the step was found.

Fail-closed details: phi edges are read before any mutation (no
partially-rewired phi on unexpected shapes); AVX2 transform arm is
unreachable!() for Max (NEON-only routing); x86 emitter falls through
to the loud unhandled-intrinsic diagnostic.

Measured: find_max 65536x2000 1.52x under qemu-aarch64 (smax-vec vs
scalar, outputs identical); 47-case edge matrix (n in {1..4096},
iv_init 0/1, both polarities, all-negative, INT_MIN seed) bit-identical
to gcc at O0/O1/O2 on ARM and x86.

Validation: 1074/1074 unit, 50/50 correctness, x86 regression 400/401
(1 = documented pre-existing check_tier2), ARM regression 0 new fails
vs baseline, fuzz 300/300 x3, ARM benchmark battery 8/8, reproducer
sweep green. New test: vectorize_max_reduction_neon.c (x86 + ARM).
